1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:05,440
Move. Transfers your approved
records into the new books.

2
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:09,200
It unlocks only when every mapping is
decided and you've approved the plan.

3
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:11,800
Records move in eight ordered batches.

4
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:15,560
Accounts, customers, vendors,
products, taxes, configuration,

5
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,380
invoices and transactions.

6
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:20,420
Each batch shows how many
of its records have moved.

7
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:25,340
If a batch hits a problem, the move
pauses there and batches already moved

8
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,760
stay moved. In the sample, batch two,

9
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:30,560
customers, pauses on a duplicate customer.

10
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,240
The card shows the cause, its
code and the retries so far.

11
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:36,700
Choose review one migration issue.

12
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:40,580
The rules propose a reversible fix
with its risk and its evidence.

13
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:45,300
Approve it, then choose retry failed
batch to rerun it from its checkpoint.

14
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,760
Reject it and the batch stays blocked.

15
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,900
Retries are limited and nothing
changes until you decide.

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,420
When every batch has moved verify
compares your old and new books.

17
00:00:55,960 --> 00:01:00,200
Harbor Light shows 17 of 17 checks
matched, eight record counts and nine

18
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,580
balance and integrity checks.

19
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:04,880
The trial balance difference
reads no difference.

20
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:09,200
A trial balance lists every account's
balance and it must agree between the

21
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,240
old and new books in exact
decimals with no tolerance and no

22
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:17,260
write-off. Open any check to see its
source, target, difference and evidence,

23
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,900
then choose continue to configuration.

24
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:24,180
Settings that need a person are listed
for your decision and each one records

25
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,560
who decided and when.

26
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,540
Next, put the new books to work.
